Forked at tag v0.1.5 (commit 24a3517e1e97670daae1ab3e76cb4b2bc48cbd17) into
core/wakeword/src/main/kotlin. Local patch: an RMS silence gate in audio/AudioRecorder.kt that
drops buffers below an energy floor before they are ever converted or emitted, so WakeWordEngine's
ONNX inference (mel-spectrogram + embedding + classifier) never runs on silence — the dominant
CPU/battery cost of always-on wake word detection (see the "VoxCommander patch" markers in that
file). The pristine upstream source is kept as a git submodule at vendor/openwakeword-android-kt.

The patch itself is maintained as a real, storable diff at
core/wakeword/patches/0001-rms-silence-gate.patch (regenerate with
scripts/regen_openwakeword_patch.sh whenever the patch changes). On an upstream release, the
scheduled sync-openwakeword.yml workflow re-vendors the sources and auto-applies this patch file —
opening a PR that's already merged + compiled + tested in the common case. It only needs a manual
merge if the patch genuinely conflicts (upstream changed the same lines), in which case the PR says
so explicitly with the reject details attached. scripts/check_openwakeword_version.sh runs the same
"would it still apply?" check locally, non-destructively.

